---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---
<Base title="Privacy · Shannon Hecker">
  <Nav />
  <main class="wrap" style="padding-top:160px;padding-bottom:100px;max-width:850px">
    <p class="eyebrow">Privacy · 10 October 2026</p>
    <h1 style="margin:24px 0 48px">Your visit, your choice.</h1>
    <h2>Optional analytics</h2>
    <p>I use Google Analytics to understand page visits, reading depth and which game levels people play. It loads only after you choose “Allow analytics”. I keep advertising features off and do not send nicknames, form entries or URL query strings to Google. Google processes technical information such as device and browser details and uses cookies to distinguish visits. Reports are private to my Analytics account.</p>
    <p>You can change your choice using Analytics settings in the footer. I remember your choice on this browser for six months. Declining does not affect the portfolio or the game. Counts reflect consenting visits, not an exact count of people.</p>
    <p><a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google’s privacy policy (opens in a new tab)</a></p>
    <h2 style="margin-top:56px">The game scoreboard</h2>
    <p>The game remembers completed stages and mission stars in this browser’s local storage. This progress stays on your device and is separate from analytics and the public scoreboard. Clearing this site’s browser data resets it.</p>
    <p>Playing does not publish your result. At the end of a stage, you can choose to share your score with an optional nickname. That nickname and score appear on the public stage scoreboard. Please use a made-up nickname, not your real name or contact details.</p>
    <p>Scores are stored with Upstash through Vercel. Each stage keeps up to 100 results, with the best ten displayed. A random run receipt prevents duplicate submissions and expires after two hours. To limit spam, a temporary keyed address digest expires after an hour; raw addresses are not stored in the scoreboard database. Vercel and Upstash also process operational data to provide their services.</p>
    <p>This is a friendly game, with basic score checks, not a competitive tournament. For removal of a score, contact me through <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/shannonhecker/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">LinkedIn (opens in a new tab)</a> with the stage, nickname and score.</p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Base>
